<title>FRANCE: Algeria buys durum, possibly Canadian - traders.</title>
<headline>Algeria buys durum, possibly Canadian - traders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria has bought 150,000 tonnes of optional-origin durum wheat at just over $200 a tonne including freight, European grain exporters said.</p>
<p>The durum maybe supplied from Canada the exporters said.</p>
<p>Shipments of 50,000 tonnes each are due in July and the first half of August.</p>
</text>
